  "reviews": [
    "The initial72-case budget controls fail12 cases on v10; native counted history witnesses distinguish limits1/2 and already-used budgets in original/one/two-copy games.",
    "The138-case comparison retains all48 earlier cases and adds24 explicit/36 keyword-static budget controls,6 all-zone metadata controls and24 life/sacrifice controls. V10 plus unchanged GameCopier fails48; v12 passes138.",
    "PowerUp synthetic flags also reduce activation costs on the entry turn. The first fixture incorrectly assumed full cost. Preserve those failures; older-permanent controls isolate budgets without weakening payment assertions. Copied older permanents still incorrectly received the discount, proving a separate copy bug. V12 preserves entry turn; all original payment assertions then pass.",
    "Metadata controls cover battlefield, hand, library, graveyard, exile and command zones, current/older turns, LKI metadata and mutation isolation. These are synthetic state contracts; keyword flags are synthetic budget contracts, not full printed-keyword rules claims.",
    "Raw inherited driver scope strings may describe earlier counts; frozen fixtures and complete method results establish the actual scope."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Installed3142-case runtime remains selected and retains the repeated-filter planning gap and newly reproduced entry-turn copy gap. The registered correction is not yet installed.",
    "The fresh candidate passes3247 native/source-parity checks. The first independent packaged attempt fails only its stale Python161-origin assertion after706 supplied method results pass; other draw groups were not run. Correct expected origin count to163 and rerun the complete packaged gate after exact-head CI. The sealed native build may be reused only with explicit proof that engine/recipe/native fixture inputs are unchanged; preserve both epochs.",
    "Fresh native build, independent packaged/origin checks, broader gameplay/serialization, full integration, catalog, installed-byte and health gates remain pending. All previous cases and resource/time budgets were retained.",
    "Found/no-plan assessment results are bounded search observations, not exhaustive legal-affordability certificates. Normal sacrifice-value strategy remains enabled.",
    "Chained filters, colored activation costs, variable-X waterbend, activation-cost modifiers (including entered-this-turn PowerUp behavior), state-dependent activation-limit expressions and user-facing assessment diagnostics need further validation.",
    "Supplied cases, source/script presence and catalog construction do not establish complete card/rules/AI support."
  ],
